Each instruction moves one hand along the ring while the other hand stays fixed. The moving hand can't pass through the fixed hand, so its cost is the linear distance between its start and target when the fixed hand's part is removed from the ring. Positions are measured from the fixed hand: `idx(x) = (x - o) mod N`, and the cost is `|idx(start) - idx(target)|`. The answer is the sum of these costs over all instructions. I checked this formula against Sample 1 (2 + 2 + 4 = 8) and then worked each case below by hand.

